# Release signing for the LED Field Visits Android app.
#
# A public release must be signed with one stable municipal key: Android refuses
# to update an installed app when the signing key changes.
#
# 1. Create the keystore once, on a machine you control:
#
#      keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore led-field-visits.jks ^
#        -alias led-field -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 9125 ^
#        -dname "CN=Sol Plaatje Municipality LED Office, O=Sol Plaatje Municipality, L=Kimberley, C=ZA"
#
# 2. Keep led-field-visits.jks and this file OUT of source control, in the
#    municipality's secret store, and back both up: losing them means you can
#    never update the app again.
#
# 3. Copy android/keystore.properties.example to android/keystore.properties and
#    fill it in, then run:  npm run apk:release
#
# storeFile=/absolute/path/to/led-field-visits.jks
# storePassword=
# keyAlias=led-field
# keyPassword=
